---
import InfoLayout from '../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

// TODO(owner): add a governing-law clause once you decide which
// jurisdiction's law should apply, and have these terms reviewed.
const updated = '2026-09-28';
---

<InfoLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Infinite Calculators"
  description="The terms for using Infinite Calculators: results are for information only, the site is provided as is, and the rules for using and linking to our content."
  h1="Terms of Use"
  updated={updated}
>
  <p>
    By using {site.name} ("the site", "we", "us") you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't
    use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the calculators</h2>
  <p>
    The calculators are free for personal and business use. You don't need an account, and you may copy,
    print or share the results you get.
  </p>

  <h2>Results are for information only</h2>
  <p>
    Results are estimates based on the values you enter and the method described on each page. They are
    not financial, tax, legal, medical, engineering or religious advice, and they are not religious
    rulings. Check any result that matters with a qualified professional or scholar before you rely on it.
    Our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> gives more detail.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We test every calculator and work to keep it correct, but the site is provided "as is" and "as
    available", without any warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or free of errors, or that
    it will always be available.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use
    of the site or your reliance on its results, including loss of money, materials, grades or time.
    Nothing in these terms limits any liability that cannot legally be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>copy or republish our pages, text, tables or code as your own</li>
    <li>scrape the site automatically, or send so many requests that it slows down for others</li>
    <li>try to break, probe or get around the site's security</li>
    <li>show our pages inside a frame on another website</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design, graphics and code on this site belong to {site.name}. You are welcome to link to any
    page without asking.
  </p>

  <h2>Ads and links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The site shows ads from third parties and links to other websites. We don't control and aren't
    responsible for their content, products or privacy practices. Seeing an ad here does not mean we
    endorse it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may change or remove calculators, and we may update these terms. The date at the top of this page
    shows when the terms last changed. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the
    updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
